## 🛠️ Step-by-Step Implementation Runbook

### Phase 1: Local Backend Engineering (VS Code)
1.  **Project Initialization:** Initialized a local backend workspace utilizing the modern **Azure Functions Node.js V4 programming model**:
    ```powershell
    & "C:\Program Files\Microsoft\Azure Functions Core Tools\func.exe" init --javascript --model V4
    ```
2.  **Endpoint Creation:** Generated a clean HTTP-triggered serverless template endpoint named `GetCloudCosts`:
    ```powershell
    & "C:\Program Files\Microsoft\Azure Functions Core Tools\func.exe" new --name GetCloudCosts --template "HTTP trigger"
    ```
3.  **SDK Integration:** Installed the official Microsoft enterprise modules to interface with the cloud identity and billing layers:
    ```bash
    npm install @azure/identity @azure/arm-costmanagement
    ```
4.  **Core Optimization Logic:** Programmed `GetCloudCosts.js` to initialize a `DefaultAzureCredential` context, query the subscription scope, fetch aggregated `ActualCost` metrics on a `Daily` granularity, and cleanly map row matrices into flat JSON data points ready for consumption by Recharts.

### Phase 2: Cloud Provisioning & DevOps (Azure CLI)
1.  **Resource Group Isolation:** Created a dedicated logical boundary to house the serverless stack:
    ```powershell
    az group create --name FinOps-Backend-RG --location eastus
    ```
2.  **State Storage Provisioning:** Automated the creation of a background storage account needed for function state tracking:
    ```powershell
    az storage account create --name magelfinopsstor --location eastus --resource-group FinOps-Backend-RG --sku Standard_LRS
    ```
3.  **Serverless Container Deployment:** Provisioned a live, fully-managed serverless container configured with Node.js 24:
    ```powershell
    az functionapp create --resource-group FinOps-Backend-RG --consumption-plan-location eastus --runtime node --runtime-version 24 --functions-version 4 --name magel-finops-api --storage-account magelfinopsstor --os-type Windows
    ```
4.  **Source Code Publishing:** Deployed local JavaScript files directly to the cloud runtime substrate using the Core Tools publisher:
    ```powershell
    & "C:\Program Files\Microsoft\Azure Functions Core Tools\func.exe" azure functionapp publish magel-finops-api
    ```

### Phase 3: Enterprise Hardening & Security (RBAC)
1.  **Environment Variable Injection:** Securely bound the target subscription ID environment flag to the live function settings:
    ```powershell
    az functionapp config appsettings set --name magel-finops-api --resource-group FinOps-Backend-RG --settings AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID="cb6fa056-2ac2-4910-8f46-04326a9a1ec2"
    ```
2.  **Managed Identity Activation:** Activated an **Entra ID System-Assigned Managed Identity**, converting the serverless computing node into a verified cryptographic security principal:
    ```powershell
    az functionapp identity assign --name magel-finops-api --resource-group FinOps-Backend-RG
    ```
3.  **Least-Privilege Role Mapping:** Implemented Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) by binding the function’s unique `principalId` strictly to the **Cost Management Reader** role, guaranteeing read-only visibility without write or delete capabilities:
    ```powershell
    az role assignment create --assignee "b1a6293f-3f4e-41d0-975b-b5f521af3c16" --role "Cost Management Reader" --scope "/subscriptions/cb6fa056-2ac2-4910-8f46-04326a9a1ec2"
    ```
4.  **Network-Level CORS Hardening:** Configured Cross-Origin Resource Sharing rules to reject all anonymous cross-domain traffic, explicitly whitelisting only the Render production frontend:
    ```powershell
    az functionapp cors add --name magel-finops-api --resource-group FinOps-Backend-RG --allowed-origins "https://onrender.com"
    ```
