## 📈 Frontend Integration Tier
The user interface reads data seamlessly by pointing standard React `useEffect` hooks directly at the serverless API layer. Because the backend pre-aggregates arrays into clean objects containing `date` and `cost` metrics, data ingestion flows smoothly into the rendering layout:

```javascript
fetch('https://azurewebsites.net')
  .then(res => res.json())
  .then(data => setCostData(data));
```

The parsed data stream is piped directly into Recharts components:
*   `<XAxis dataKey="date" />` maps chronological billing points.
*   `<Bar dataKey="cost" fill="#007fff" />` renders scalable, color-coded expenditure bars.

